    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nWhen enabling contents preview for registers via `MiniClue.gen_clues.registers({ show_contents = true })`, invoking register completion (e.g. via `<C-r>` or `<C-r><C-o>` in Insert mode) generates clues for all available registers, including empty ones. This causes the `mini.clue` floating window to stretch across full height of the screen, filled mostly with empty entries.\n\nIt would be nice to have an option to filter out that registers. Example:\n```lua\nMiniClue.gen_clues.registers({\n  show_contents = true,\n  hide_empty = true,\n})\n```\n",
